  THE PROTOCOL IS NOT THE CEILING, ON THIS RAMP (-1.0 SE). Walking the
  target out reaches the same place as demanding it at once, which points
  the limit back at the voice rather than at the reward's blindness, and
  would revive `ceiling-is-an-exponent`: dF1 ~ aligned^0.61, and no amount
  of asking more carefully changes an exponent.

  BUT THIS NULL IS AMBIGUOUS, AND THE AMBIGUITY WAS WRITTEN DOWN BEFORE THE
  RUN. The ramp moves 0.00122 log units per trial. If that outran the voice,
  the creature stopped straddling partway up and the later trials were back
  in exactly the invariant regime `travelsweep` measured -- in which case
  this tested a ramp that was too fast, not the idea of ramping. The two
  readings are distinguished by a SLOWER ramp, and that is the follow-up a
  null here buys: ramp over the whole session and score the last tenth.
  Do not retire the protocol explanation on this result alone.
